#
# Line endings are declared here instead of being left to each clone's
# core.autocrlf setting, because the two script families in this repository
# have opposite, non-negotiable requirements.
#
# cmd.exe cannot parse a batch file with LF endings. It does not fail cleanly:
# it drops the first character of some lines, so REM is executed as EM, for as
# or, and if as f. A skipped line in settings.bat leaves ROOT_DIR empty and
# every derived path collapses to the drive root.
#
# The *.sh helpers have the mirror-image requirement: a CR at the end of a
# shebang or a variable makes bash report $'\r': command not found.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no "* text=auto", which would renormalise the whole
# tree and bury real changes under a whitespace diff.

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.sh text eol=lf
